From: Tiaoge-tou <85100527+Tiaoge-tou@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:27:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Display rate above 60: the measured-rate mode across present,
 fpslock, vsync and the front end

The 120 Hz display-rate mode (patch port 0067, group O of the port inventory), carried from the Tiaoge-tou/nxnative fork, with both games' display_hz rows.

hle_nvn.c defines dm_display_hz / dm_display_set_hz (declared in patch 0065): the front end's measured rate drives the present tick, and the handheld stale-crop fix in nvnWindowSetCrop rides along (its DM_DIAG_STATE_OFF readback, a bisect diagnostic, is not carried: the green-screen switch group stays out of this queue). nvn_mtl.m switches the present link to 120 Hz while the mode is driven and counts intervals and vsyncs at the driven rate. hle_sdk16.c ticks the vi vsync event at the measured rate. hle_fpslock.c gains the Silksong row (Unity targetFrameRate, an int32 field) and the display-rate servo for int32 fields only: the measured rate overwrites the game's -1 sentinel while driven and the -1 goes back on release; with no fixed target the tick now continues for such rows instead of stopping, and a double field is never written without a fixed target. This tree has no dynamically scanned rows, so the kind test is the servo's eligibility test.

front_ios.m completes the wiring this queue owes from earlier groups: it publishes the measured render sizes (DM_RENDER_WIDTH / DM_RENDER_WIDTH_HD, the front half of patch 0065's host service), measures the screen rate for the launcher's frame-rate choice (SS_DISPLAY_HZ, including the lowered 1912x880 tier) and hands it to the host, and carries the Hades II HUD script fix, the front-end half of patch 0064's group.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: 120 Hz display-rate mode for Silksong and Hades II, paced by the measured screen rate (PROJECT.md Phase 2)
Issue: Tiaoge-tou/NX2Apple PROJECT.md Phase 2

